    <innerclass refid="structterminal_1_1_winsize" prot="public">terminal::Winsize</innerclass>
    <innernamespace refid="namespaceterminal">terminal</innernamespace>
    <briefdescription>
<para>Packed terminal viewport dimensions — cell + pixel in one atomic <ref refid="group__juce__core-maths_1gaba41bf2b6f6da5945ee08fb99931aede" kindref="member" external="/Users/jreng/Documents/Poems/JUCE/docs/doxygen/doc/juce.tag">uint64</ref>. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><computeroutput><ref refid="structterminal_1_1_winsize" kindref="compound">terminal::Winsize</ref></computeroutput> mirrors POSIX <computeroutput>struct winsize</computeroutput>: terminal dimensions in both cell units (cols, rows) and physical pixels (pixelWidth, pixelHeight).</para>
<para>Display is the sole author. All consumers read from a single Parameter&lt;int64_t&gt; via pack()/unpack(). Four 16-bit fields packed into one int64_t — one atomic store, one atomic load, zero drift.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="see"><para>Display::resized() — computes and publishes Winsize </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="class_t_t_y_1a61a7a6b2d7043f97c299ae6ae76ff361" kindref="member">TTY::setWinsize()</ref> — consumes <ref refid="jam__cell_8h_1adb968df47f8b9dd5aa6a35499c35c9f6" kindref="member" external="/Users/jreng/Documents/Poems/dev/jam/doxygen/tagfile.xml">cell</ref> + pixel dims for SIGWINCH </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
